            "text": "{\"study_topic_id\":\"study-14fd3bb12e237c98bd3b\",\"overview\":{\"text\":\"Isabel Allende is a novelist and memoirist born in Lima to Chilean parents and raised mostly in Chile. After the 1973 military coup, she went into exile in Venezuela; there, a letter to her dying grandfather grew into her first novel, The House of the Spirits (1982). The novel brought her wide recognition and blends family history and political upheaval with supernatural elements, following generations of women. Across her fiction, Allende connects personal lives with historical change and often centers women challenging restrictive expectations. The House of the Spirits, Daughter of Fortune, and Portrait in Sepia form a trilogy, though each novel can be read independently.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/authors/417/isabel-allende/\",\"https://www.nationalbook.org/people/isabel-allende/\",\"https://www.isabelallende.com/en/words/wandering_spirits\"]},\"key_facts\":[{\"text\":\"Allende was born in Lima in 1942 to Chilean parents and grew up mostly in Chile.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://www.isabelallende.com/en/words/wandering_spirits\",\"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/authors/417/isabel-allende/\"]},{\"text\":\"After Chile’s 1973 coup, she lived in exile in Caracas, Venezuela.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://www.isabelallende.com/en/words/wandering_spirits\",\"https://www.nationalbook.org/people/isabel-allende/\"]},{\"text\":\"A letter she began to her dying grandfather became the basis of The House of the Spirits, published in 1982.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://www.nationalbook.org/people/isabel-allende/\",\"https://www.isabelallende.com/en/words/wandering_spirits\"]},{\"text\":\"The House of the Spirits combines a multigenerational family saga with Chilean political history and magical elements.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://www.isabelallende.com/en/words/wandering_spirits\",\"https://www.nationalbook.org/people/isabel-allende/\"]},{\"text\":\"The House of the Spirits, Daughter of Fortune, and Portrait in Sepia are linked novels that can each be read on its own.\",\"source_urls\":[\"https://www.isabelallende.com/en/words/wandering_spirits\"]}],\"sources\":[{\"title\":\"Isabel Allende\",\"url\":\"https://www.penguinrandomhouse.com/authors/417/isabel-allende/\",\"publisher\":\"Penguin Random House\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-09-24T18:37:37.392951+00:00\",\"supports\":\"Author biography: born in Peru and raised in Chile; lists major works including The House of the Spirits and Eva Luna.\"},{\"title\":\"Isabel Allende\",\"url\":\"https://www.nationalbook.org/people/isabel-allende/\",\"publisher\":\"National Book Foundation\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-09-24T18:37:37.392951+00:00\",\"supports\":\"Biographical and literary context: 1973 coup and exile, origin and 1982 publication of The House of the Spirits, its family-and-history scope, and Allende’s literary recognition.\"},{\"title\":\"The Wandering Spirits of Isabel Allende\",\"url\":\"https://www.isabelallende.com/en/words/wandering_spirits\",\"publisher\":\"Stanford Libraries essay by Adán Griego, hosted on Isabel Allende’s official website\",\"retrieved_at\":\"2026-09-24T18:37:37.392951+00:00\",\"supports\":\"Birth and upbringing, exile, the letter that became her debut novel, the novel’s blend of magical and real elements, and the independently readable trilogy.\"}],\"research_queries\":[\"Isabel Allende biography official website author Chilean American The House of the Spirits\",\"Isabel Allende biography National Women's History Museum\",\"Isabel Allende biography Britannica novels magical realism\"],\"notes\":\"Overview is one paragraph of 100 words. Each key fact and substantive overview claim has supporting source URLs. Search-result pages that could not be opened were not used as sources.\",\"unresolved_concerns\":[],\"self_check_complete\":true}"
